'' ONE DIRECTORY SPELLED IN ANOTHER CASE IS ONE KEY on Windows (modcache.bas, KeyPath_). The
'' editor passes '.../Toolchains/...' and a shell '.../toolchains/...'; the key held the path
'' as written, so the second spelling missed and every module was rebuilt -- ~15 s for fbx.gui
'' -- although its object was already cached. The second build spells the include path and
'' the source in upper case and must hit both modules.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.mct-case/cache
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.mct-case
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/modcache => build/.mct-case
'' STEP: -v -target windows-x86_64 -i build/.mct-case/libs build/.mct-case/app/main.bas -o build/.mct-case/app.exe
'' STEP-OUT: module acme.leaf: miss (new)
'' STEP-OUT: module acme.middle: miss (new)
'' ARGS: -v -target windows-x86_64 -i BUILD/.MCT-CASE/LIBS BUILD/.MCT-CASE/APP/MAIN.BAS -o build/.mct-case/app.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.leaf: hit
'' EXPECT-OUT: module acme.middle: hit
'' EXPECT-NOT: miss
'' RUN: build/.mct-case/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  14
